{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the people were as complainers.</b> From the language of (Lamentations 3:39) ״מה יתאונן אדם חי״ — for they were aggrieved and suffering now that they had entered the wilderness, and this complaining was evil in the ears of HaShem because they did not go joyfully but under compulsion and with worry. And it says כמתאוננים — 'as complainers' — with the כ of resemblance, to indicate that they muttered this among themselves and did not express it openly, out of fear of Moses lest he hear; therefore it says וישמע ה׳ — 'and HaShem heard' — that is, and not Moses."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:07.316658438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}